For an international organization in New York, we are urgently looking for a REMOTE (Senior) QA Manager for .NET and Angular-based applications. The QA Manager should be experienced with a history of working in an agile environment. Candidates must have hands-on experience working with Angular, .NET, MS SQL in teams building large consumer-facing web applications from the ground up.

Candidates need to be fluent in English. All positions are long-term. This position is open for freelancers and employees.

Candidates need to be able to work normal office hours in New York, US. Example 9 AM NY time equals 7:30 PM

Tasks and Responsibilities:

• Work within an agile team to ensure the quality of complex .NET and Angular based Web and mobile applications;

• Test applications in multilingual setup;

• Execute functional test scripts and analyze bugs for systems in development;

• Perform manual testing on a variety of browsers and operating systems using manual and with tools like browser stack;

• Work closely with developers and DevOps teams to recognize the potential for any operational issues, assess risks, and resolve issues proactively;

• Perform load testing using a variety of tools as per industry standards and suggest solutions for performance issues;

• Perform API testing using Postman and similar tools;

• Record defect details and create reports outlining the types of defects found and the steps taken to resolve them and update the regression test framework;

• Maintain knowledgebase documentation in SharePoint;

Profile:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• 8+ years of experience in Quality Assurance for complex web applications;

• 5+ years in leading a team of QA with a combination of manual, load, automation, and accessibility testers;

• 5+ years in performing manual, security, integration, API, end-to-end, load, automation, mobile application, and accessibility testing;

• 5+ years of experience in providing clearance emails for UAT and PROD releases;

• 3+ years of experience in leading QA for multilingual applications;

• 3+ years of experience using JMeter, BlazeMeter, Browser stack;

• Experience in creating and executing scripted test cases;

• Experience with Mobile application testing, browser compatibility, and accessibility testing experience;

• Experience in identifying, analyzing, documenting, and maintaining test results;

• Experience in writing SQL queries (DQL);

• Exposure to GitLab, Azure DevOps, and CI/CD pipelines;

• Good interpersonal skills to work with developers in an agile environment;

• Experience with MS Teams and SharePoint documentation is a plus;

• ISTQB or similar certification is a plus;

• English language proficiency (oral and written);

Offered:

• A Challenging role for an international organization in New York;

• Attractive salary package;

Interested:

